# West Coast Clothing Co. — Development Rules & Stack Standards

## Tech Stack & Core Dependencies
- Framework: Next.js 15 (App Router, Server Components by default)
- UI / Styling: Tailwind CSS, Lucide React icons (`lucide-react@^0.444.0`)
- Markdown Rendering: `react-markdown` (`^10.1.0`)
- Backend & Auth: Supabase (`@supabase/supabase-js`)
- Deployment: Vercel auto-deploys from GitHub `main` branch

## Project Architecture & Routing
- `app/page.tsx`: Catalog homepage / product grid
- `app/products/[slug]/page.tsx`: Dynamic Product Detail Page (PDP)
- `app/Header.tsx`: Global navigation header
- `app/layout.tsx`: Root layout shell
- `app/globals.css`: Global Tailwind styles & font declarations

## Supabase Schema: `products`
Columns expected on the `products` table:
- `id` (uuid)
- `title` (text)
- `slug` (text, unique)
- `description` (text, formatted with Markdown / bullet lists)
- `image_url` (text)
- `affiliate_url` (text)
- `brand` (text, e.g. "Patagonia", "Brixton")
- `retailer` (text, e.g. "REI", "Backcountry")
- `tags` (array of text)

## Design System & UI Conventions
- Primary Accent: `emerald-800` (hover: `emerald-900`) for CTAs, retailer tags, and brand badges.
- Neutral Palette: Clean white containers (`bg-white border border-neutral-200 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm`) over light neutral backgrounds (`bg-neutral-50` / `bg-neutral-100`).
- Typography: Clean sans-serif hierarchy; subtext/metadata using `text-xs font-semibold text-neutral-500`.
- Rich Text Formatting: Always wrap product descriptions in `<ReactMarkdown>` with custom component overrides for unordered lists (`ul`), list items (`li`), and paragraphs (`p`).
